Supplier profiles in this folder
================================

Source: TED (Tenders Electronic Daily), the online version of the Supplement to the
Official Journal of the EU, https://ted.europa.eu, fetched through its search API.

Content of panel.jsonl.gz: one profile for each of the 200 panel suppliers, built from
the award notices published before 1 April 2026 that name the supplier as a winner.
A profile holds category codes with weights, buyer countries, hashed buyer ids, a count
of past wins, and up to 40 excerpts of award-notice text (title and description, cut
at 600 characters): 5,550 excerpts in all, as the API returned them. The excerpts
describe the contract. They can name the buying organisation; they do not hold the
winner's name, and no contact field was ever requested.

Content of aliases.json: for each panel supplier, a hash of every spelling of its name
or registration number, mapped to its profile id. It lets the scheduled run recognise
a panel supplier in a new award without the names being in the repository.

The ids are hashes, not anonymity. Award notices are public, the hash is unsalted and
its recipe is in the source code, so anyone who has a supplier's name can compute its
id, and the contract excerpts can be searched on TED. The hashes keep a list of company
names out of this repository; they do not hide who the suppliers are from someone who
goes looking.

Reuse: the TED legal notice states that procurement notices "can be freely reused, for
commercial or non-commercial purposes", under the Commission Decision of 12 December
2011 on the reuse of Commission documents (read on 2026-11-17 at
https://ted.europa.eu/en/legal-notice). (c) European Union.
